.TH API-BALANCE 1 "September 2026" "api-balance 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
api-balance \- query and monitor AI API balances and quotas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B api-balance
[\fIcheck\fR|\fIwatch\fR|\fIproviders\fR|\fIconfig\fR|\fIversion\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B api-balance
is a lightweight CLI for querying balances and quotas across multiple AI API
providers (DeepSeek, OpenRouter, SiliconFlow, Moonshot/Kimi, MiniMax, and
user-defined custom providers). It can run continuously in watch mode and
send alerts to Telegram or a webhook when a balance or quota drops below a
configured threshold.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B api-balance check [--json]
Query all configured providers and print their balances/quotas.
Add \fB--json\fR for machine-readable JSON output.
.TP
.B api-balance watch [--interval DURATION] [--once]
Run the monitoring loop. The first check runs immediately, then repeats every
\fIinterval\fR (default 30m). \fB--once\fR runs a single check + evaluate, useful
for testing.
.TP
.B api-balance providers
List built-in providers and their stability.
.TP
.B api-balance config validate [--config PATH]
Validate the configuration file.
.TP
.B api-balance version
Print the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Default search paths (lowest precedence first):
.br
/etc/api-balance/config.yaml
.br
~/.config/api-balance/config.yaml
.PP
API keys are read from environment variables named by \fBapi_key_env\fR, or from
an inline \fBapi_key\fR field (discouraged; use chmod 600 on the config).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Provider keys are read via the \fBapi_key_env\fR name. In systemd service mode,
keys may be placed in /etc/api-balance/api-balance.env (chmod 600).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on configuration/provider errors, 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)